{
  "_readme": "International tourism numbers for every African country. Arrivals and receipts come from the UN Tourism Statistics Database (bulk download, data to 2024); where UN Tourism has no figure for a country, the older World Bank Open Data figure is kept. GDP and population come from World Bank Open Data. A null value means no figure has been reported, never a zero. Every number carries its own reporting year, shown to the reader, because years differ by country. Do not backfill or estimate a missing value. arrivals uses UN Tourism's 'all visitors' series (the one the World Bank figures followed), or the 'overnight visitors' series where that is the only or the more recent one; arrivals.basis records which. receipts_usd is inbound expenditure, travel plus passenger transport where reported, else travel only (receipts_usd.basis). receipts_pct_gdp divides receipts by that country's GDP in the same year. spend_per_arrival_usd divides receipts for the arrivals year by arrivals, and is null when receipts for that year are missing. population is the country's total population in its own reporting year. arrivals_trend compares the arrivals figure with 2019 where 2019 is 4 to 7 years earlier, else with the closest year 4 to 7 years earlier, never 2020 or 2021, and is null when there is no such year or when the arrivals figure itself is older than 2019. Regenerate with node scripts/generate-tourism-data.mjs after refreshing the underlying data in this file.",
